@tedpar I linked the issue as it is related. I am not claiming it is the exact same issue. 

> The proper fix would be to adhere to CLDR parseLenient data,

That would be risky breaking change. Even ICU when parsing numbers making this as opt-in behavior to allow lenient parsing. But I think we can have some middle ground here which we can find out if the culture using any of the alternative minus signs, then we'll allow the hyphen U+002D for such locale. I believe this will address all concerns here.
